{
  "bio": [
    "Rick Workman is the founder and chairman of Heartland Dental, the largest dental support organization in the U.S. with more than 1,900 offices in 39 states.",
    "He founded Heartland in 1997 after selling a 29 office practice that same year for $15.8 million.",
    "Private equity giant KKR took a 58% stake in Heartland in 2018 at a $2.8 billion valuation.",
    "In 2024, Heartland had $3.6 billion in revenue and $455 million in earnings.",
    "In 2025, became a minority owner of the Tampa Bay Rays major league baseball team."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Raised on a farm in Clay County, Illinois. Comes from a family of farmers and teachers. His mother was one of his grade school teachers."
  ]
